  "normalize": false,
  "sentence_method": "one complete sentence per generation",
  "word_method": "independent word generation, not extracted from sentence audio",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "When Albert Einstein was 16 years old, he imagined himself riding alongside a beam of light.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-01.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "He used this picture in mind to help him when working out the theory of relativity.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-02.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Daydreaming, called Thought Experiments by Einstein, can make you have wild imaginings.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-03.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "We can imagine different landscapes, like mountains and forests.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-04.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "It lets your mind walk slowly around things that aren't happening right now.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-05.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "It means thinking ahead to a holiday or a birthday party.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-06.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "text": "Disappearing into a daydream lets your mind escape when things are difficult.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-07.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "text": "It helps you deal with worries and fears.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-08.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "text": "For example, imagining how you're going to speak up in class is like practising the scene in your head, which can make you feel calmer.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-09.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "text": "Imagining graduating encourages you to work harder towards your learning goals.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-10.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "text": "Reading literature also inspires our creativity in daydreaming.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-11.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "text": "When we picture ourselves as a princess or a queen wearing a beautiful dress, we let our minds wander in a fairy tale that brings us courage.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-12.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "text": "Then we may pick up our pens to write our own paragraphs.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-13.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "text": "However, try not to let your mind be absent when you need to focus in class or cross the road.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-14.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "text": "Instead, find a time when you don't have to focus on anything, like going for a walk or brushing your teeth.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-15.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "text": "Research shows that people often come up with more solutions to problems after daydreaming because it is similar to staying at a hotel, where we can take a break.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-16.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "text": "So next time you're stuck on homework, stop for a moment and see where your daydreams take you.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-17.mp3",
      "exists": true
    }
  ],
